  "identifier": "cod-bo7-season-02-weapon-tier-2026-02",
  "headline": "Call of Duty: Black Ops 7 Season 2 Weapon Tier Guide (6v6 Multiplayer)",
  "description": "Tiered weapon guide for Season 2 based on the 2026-02-13 patch notes, covering Assault Rifles, SMGs, LMGs, Marksman, Shotgun, Sniper, Handgun, Special, and Launcher.",
  "articleBody": "This guide summarizes the Season 2 balance changes in Call of Duty: Black Ops 7 patch notes (2026-02-13), with an emphasis on 6v6 multiplayer.\n\nSources used\n- Call of Duty: Black Ops 7 Season 02 Patch Notes\n- Call of Duty: Warzone Season 02 Patch Notes\n- Community tier snapshots referenced for practical meta placement\n\nBase Rule\n- Tier ranking is built from official weapon tuning impact first, then adjusted by early Season 2 6v6 performance signals.\n\n【S Tier】\n- AR: EGRT-17, DS20 Mirage\n  - EGRT-17: recoil control improved (Vertical Recoil Control 50→40%, Recoil Gun Kick 49→39).\n  - DS20 Mirage: max damage range expanded and 17.1\" Abdicator barrel recoil reduced; launcher got meaningful QoL (171→240 RPM and burst delay 300→200 ms).\n- SMG: REV-46\n  - REV-46 keeps top-class close pressure with headshot multiplier increased to 1.28x and versatile folding-stock handling.\n- LMG: Sokol 545\n  - Extra neck-damage tuning and attachment mobility/accuracy buffs (including Parallel Foregrip ADS spread and ADS-movement gains).\n- Marksman: M8A1\n  - Recoil control reduced substantially (VRC 55→35, gun kick 49→32).\n\n【A Tier】\n- AR: AK-27, Peacekeeper Mk1\n  - AK-27 now handles significantly better for mid-range work (VRC/Gun Kick 50→35).\n  - Peacekeeper Mk1 received strong recoil control and fire-rate improvements.\n- SMG: Razor 9mm, Carbon 57, Ryden 45K\n  - Razor/Carbon received major recoil reductions (45→30 on both axes).\n  - Ryden gained stability on jump-landing transitions.\n- LMG: XM325\n  - Attachment quality improved in multiple points (better handling and recoil on key barrels/stocks and 15%→35% recoil control improvements on key modules).\n- Sniper: Hawker HX, VS Recon\n  - Both got flinch-system adjustments; they stay usable but require more deliberate attachment setup and timing.\n- Shotgun: M10 Breacher\n  - Sprint-to-fire timing was improved with the prestige stock.\n- Handgun: Velox 5.7, CODA 9\n  - Both guns improved practical consistency through stronger vertical recoil reduction and fire-rate gains.\n\n【B Tier】\n- AR: X9 Maverick\n  - Jump/landing stability buff helps aggression, but range/value remains below top ARs.\n- SMG: MPC-25\n  - Prestige barrel and laser penalty adjustments improve mid-range consistency, though still less dominant in pure 1v1 spam environments.\n- Marksman: M34 Novaline, Warden 308\n  - M34 Novaline recoil control improved, while Warden 308 lost default hold-breath behavior (melee interaction/tempo changed).\n- Sniper: XR-3 Ion, Shadow SK\n  - Usable with careful positioning; mostly trade handling for control after flinch and ADS-speed tuning.\n- Launcher: A.R.C. M1\n  - No combat stat upgrade; functional issue fixes only.\n\n【C Tier】\n- AR: Maddox RFB\n  - Mid-to-long range engagement became harder without recoil attachments.\n- SMG: --\n- LMG: MK.78\n  - ADS spread behavior restored and damage taper adjusted down; still strong in raw output but less forgiving.\n- Handgun: --\n- Special: GDL Havoc\n  - Reserve ammo and airburst radius were reduced, lowering sustained spam and raw area dominance.\n\n【D Tier】\n- Sniper: XR-3 Ion (inconsistent map fit after ADS/attachment shifts)\n- Handgun: --\n- Launcher/Special: GDL and ARC remain utility tools rather than mainline staples if you do not build around their strengths.\n\nBottom line\n- BO7 Season 2 strongly rewards stable burst, controlled recoil, and disciplined positioning.\n- If you want first-pick consistency in 6v6, prioritize DS20 Mirage / EGRT-17 style ARs and the corrected Sokol 545 style LMG profile; treat high-damage long-range pick styles as more build-dependent.\n",
  "articleSection": "game-guide",
